ATA_JSON with agent \"agent_2\". So we are agent_2. We need to produce a public message as agent_2, referencing the discussion, and give a vote.\n\nWe have already given a public message earlier as agent_2 recommending C. Now we need to respond again? The conversation is at round 3, agent 3 just gave a message. Now it's agent 2's turn again. We need to produce a new contribution. We need to consider the current state: Agent 1 recommended A, Agent 3 recommended B, Agent 2 previously recommended C (and reaffirmed). Now we need to respond, perhaps adjust our vote or keep C. We need to reference prior discussion. We can either maintain C or shift. Let's evaluate.\n\nWe have candidate facts. We need to decide which candidate is best overall. Let's weigh:\n\n- Candidate C: 100% reliability, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Also we have \"understands complicated technology\" and \"excellent attention skills\". So technical competence is good. The communication difficulty and egocentric attitude could affect crew cooperation. But positive crew atmosphere suggests good cooperation. The egocentric may be mitigated.\n\n- Candidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, pretentious tone, makes nasty remarks, uncooperative. So reliability and stress resilience are strong, but communication issues are serious.\n\n- Candidate A: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized, regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas, unfriendly. So technical competence and leadership are strong, but reliability and cooperation concerns.\n\n- Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as a know-it-all, hot temper, considered a loner, weak leadership. So responsibility and problem solving are strong, but cooperation and attitude issues.\n\nWe need to pick best overall. The panel is split. As agent_2, we can either maintain C or shift. Let's consider: C's reliability and decision quality are top. Crew atmosphere positive suggests good cooperation despite communication difficulty. Egocentric may be a concern but perhaps less severe than B's nasty remarks. A's unorganized and not open to new ideas could affect adaptability. D's hot temper and loner also problematic.\n\nThus C seems strongest overall. So we can keep vote C, but we need to respond to Agent 3's argument for B and Agent 1's for A. We can argue that C's reliability and decision quality outweigh B's communication issues and A's reliability concerns. Also note that C's positive crew atmosphere mitigates communication difficulty. So we keep C.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I still recommend Candidate C because ...\". Then METADATA_JSON with agent \"agent_2\" and vote \"Candidate C\".\n\nMake sure format: PUBLIC_MESSAGE: then newline then the message, then METADATA_JSON: newline then JSON.\n\nProceed."}
