 C: reliability, quick decisions, positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric. Candidate A: technical and leadership, but unorganized and not good at criticism. Candidate B: conscientious, stress handling, but pretentious tone.\n\nWhich is best? The safety-critical role values reliability, decision quality, stress resilience, crew cooperation. C has reliability and decision quality, and positive crew atmosphere suggests cooperation. Communication difficulty may be mitigated. So C seems best.\n\nThus as Agent 1, we can change our vote to Candidate C, acknowledging Agent 2's points and arguing that C's strengths outweigh A's concerns. Provide evidence: 100% reliability, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere. Mention that A's unorganized and criticism issues are more concerning for reliability.\n\nThus we will vote for Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I now see that Candidate C's reliability and decision quality, plus positive crew atmosphere, outweigh A's technical strengths, so I shift my recommendation to C.\" Provide reasoning.\n\nThen METADATA_JSON with agent \"agent_1\" and vote \"Candidate C\".\n\nMake sure format: PUBLIC_MESSAGE: then newline then message, then METADATA_JSON: newline then JSON.\n\nProceed."}
